Name [SimTalk] - cells
Sets the name of the sublist or subtable contained in the addressed cell of the list/table designated by
<Path>.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path-of-the-list[row]>.Name.string
<Path-of-the-table[column,row]>.Name.string
Return Value
The return value has the data type string.
Example
DataTable.createNestedList(1, 1, "abc")
print DataTable[1,1].Name  // prints "abc"
DataTable[1,1].Name := "XY"
print DataTable[1,1].Name  // prints "XY" 
Name [SimTalk] - cells
Plant Simulation Help 11-4061
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Void [SimTalk] - cells of lists/tables
Returns if specified cell of the list/table designated by <Path> is empty (true) or not (false).
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path-of-the-list[row]>.void -> boolean
<Path-of-the-table[column,row]>.void -> boolean
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
if not DataTable[1,1].void
   DataTable[1,1] += 1
end
Read-Only Attributes of Lists and Tables
_Read-Only Attributes of Lists and Tables
Lists and tables provide the read-only attributes listed in the table of contents to the left for returning their
state.
You can query the values of the read-only attributes, but you cannot set them as Plant Simulation
computes the value for the point-in-time at which you query it. In most cases a read-only attribute
corresponds to an unavailable dialog item on one of the tabs of the object, for example on the tab
Statistics.
To view all of the methods, read-only attributes, and attributes of the object, open the window Show
Attributes and Methods. The figure below illustrates the information using the example of the object
Station.
